# Real time

- Clock callbacks and `RtObject::tick` are `noexcept`. No `new`, `malloc`, `make_shared`, `push_back`, `std::string` growth, locks, or I/O.
- Publish a new snapshot from the message thread. The clock only loads the pointer and acknowledges the generation it finished.
- `RtChannel` is for trivially copyable values. If a value does not fit, the push fails; the caller does not allocate a fallback on the clock thread.
- Do not read or write `Document` from a tick.

```cpp
void GroupSnapshot::tick(const xen::TickInfo&) noexcept {
    ++ticks_; // already allocated; no heap growth
}
```
